The Fibonacci sequence is a series of numbers in which each number is the sum of the two preceding ones, starting from 0 and 1. The n-th Fibonacci number can be calculated using dynamic programming by computing the n-1st and n-2nd Fibonacci numbers and adding them together. For example, the 5th Fibonacci number is calculated as follows: F5 = F4 + F3 = 3 + 2 = 5. Therefore, the program can be written as follows: 
int Fibonacci(int n) { 
    if (n == 0 || n == 1) 
        return n; 
    else    
        return Fibonacci(n - 1) + Fibonacci(n - 2); 
